<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/canada"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Canada.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Canada</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Canada acquires Rupert’s Land and creates the province of Manitoba</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/french-algeria"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/French%20Algeria.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>French Algeria</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Crémieux Decree grants French citizenship to Algerian Jews</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/papal-states"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Papal%20States.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Papal States</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Italian troops enter Rome through the breach at Porta Pia</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-italy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Italy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Italy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Italian troops take Rome from the Papal States</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bunyoro"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Bunyoro.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Bunyoro</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Kabalega wins the throne and builds the standing abarusura army</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/theocracy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Theocracy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Theocracy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Italian troops take Rome on 20 September, ending the Papal States</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/impressionism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Impressionism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Impressionism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Frédéric Bazille dies in the Franco-Prussian War</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/french-third-republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/French%20Third%20Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>French Third Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Parisian deputies led by Léon Gambetta establish the Government of National Defence</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/rome"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Rome.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Rome</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Italian troops enter through Porta Pia, and Rome becomes capital of Italy in 1871</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-koniggratz"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20K%C3%B6niggr%C3%A4tz.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Königgrätz</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">War with France, in whose background lay the French demand for revenge for Sadová</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-sedan-1870"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Sedan%20(1870).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Sedan (1870)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">After a hard-fought French defeat at Gravelotte on 18 August, Bazaine's Army of the Rhine retreats to Metz and is besieged there from 19 August</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-sedan-1870"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Sedan%20(1870).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Sedan (1870)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 23 August the new Army of Châlons begins a left-flanking march north-east towards the Belgian border to relieve Metz</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-sedan-1870"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Sedan%20(1870).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Sedan (1870)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 30 August the Prussian Fourth Army defeats MacMahon at Beaumont, and he withdraws towards Sedan</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-sedan-1870"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Sedan%20(1870).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Sedan (1870)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 31 August the French deploy around Sedan while Moltke arranges his armies to encircle them</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-sedan-1870"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Sedan%20(1870).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Sedan (1870)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 1 September the Germans attack from several sides, take Bazeilles, drive the French into the Bois de la Garenne and defeat the breakout attempts</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-sedan-1870"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Sedan%20(1870).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Sedan (1870)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 2 September Wimpffen signs the surrender of the Army of Châlons and the fortress of Sedan</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-sedan-1870"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Sedan%20(1870).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Sedan (1870)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 4 September the Second Empire collapses in a bloodless revolution and a Government of National Defence is proclaimed</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-sedan-1870"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Sedan%20(1870).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Sedan (1870)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 19 September the Prussian Third and Fourth Armies begin the siege of Paris</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/vladimir-lenin"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Vladimir%20Lenin.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Vladimir Lenin</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Vladimir Ilyich Ulyanov is born in Simbirsk</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/unification-of-italy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Unification%20of%20Italy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Unification of Italy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Italian army breaches the Aurelian Walls at Porta Pia and enters Rome</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/jehovahs-witnesses"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Jehovah's%20Witnesses.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Jehovah's Witnesses</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Charles Taze Russell and others form a Bible study group in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania</span></li></ul></section>
